{
  "dom_id": "step-q103840",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "If $cot\u2061x=\\sqrt{2}$ for some $x,$ then find the value of $cot\u2061(x-9\\pi ).$",
  "worked_solution": "The period of $y=cot\u2061x$ is $\\pi .$ Therefore, for any integer $n,$ we have\n\n$$\ncot\u2061x=cot\u2061(x+n\\pi ).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $n=-9$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}cot\u2061x & =cot\u2061(x+(-9)\\cdot \\pi ) \\\\  & =cot\u2061(x-9\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, if $cot\u2061x=\\sqrt{2},$ then $cot\u2061(x-9\\pi )=\\sqrt{2}.$",
